# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in your own values.
# backend/.env is already covered by .gitignore (.env and .env.*) — never commit it.

# Google Maps JavaScript API key. This is the ONLY Google credential this app uses —
# there is no separate Places/Geocoding key. In Google Cloud Console, enable these APIs
# for the project this key belongs to:
#   - Maps JavaScript API  (renders the map — required)
#   - Places API           (origin/destination autocomplete + nearby hospitals — required)
#   - Directions API       (real road routes — required; also resolves plain-text
#                           origin/destination, so a separate Geocoding API is not called
#                           directly by this app)
# Without all three enabled, the map itself will still render, but autocomplete,
# directions and nearby-hospital lookups will fail with a visible in-app error message
# rather than fail silently or fall back to a different map engine.
#
# The key IS sent to the browser at runtime (that is how the Google Maps JS API
# works for every app that uses it) — it is not a secret in the server-side sense.
# It is protected by restricting it in Google Cloud Console to your domain(s)
# (HTTP referrer restriction) and to only the specific Maps APIs you enable, not by
# hiding it. Leaving it out of this repo just prevents it being restriction-less and
# world-usable by anyone who clones the repo.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
